# This repo holds Linux shell/Python scripts that boot on SystemRescue -
# they must always have Unix (LF) line endings, never Windows (CRLF).
#
# Without this file, Windows git installs commonly convert LF to CRLF on
# checkout (the core.autocrlf=true default many Windows git installers
# suggest). A CRLF line ending on a script's #!/bin/bash shebang line breaks
# it outright - Linux tries to run the interpreter "/bin/bash\r", which
# doesn't exist, and the script fails to execute at all with a
# "No such file or directory" error, before it ever gets a chance to run.
#
# This forces LF regardless of anyone's local git configuration.
* text=auto eol=lf
